INSERT INTO t_null VALUES(1, 'insert');

1 row in set. Elapsed: 0.014 sec.
```

Clickhouse inner join has an optimization to join with empty tables:

```sql
CREATE TABLE left ( A UInt64,B String ) ENGINE = MergeTree ORDER BY A as 
SELECT number, toString(cityHash64(number)) FROM numbers(100000000);

CREATE TABLE right ( A UInt64, B String ) ENGINE = MergeTree ORDER BY A;

select count() from left inner join right using A;

1 row in set. Elapsed: 0.010 sec. Processed 261.64 thousand rows, 2.09 MB (27.24 million rows/s., 217.93 MB/s.)


insert  into right SELECT number, toString(cityHash64(number)) FROM numbers(1);

select count() from left inner join right using A;
1 row in set. Elapsed: 0.367 sec. Processed 100.00 million rows, 800.00 MB (272.51 million rows/s., 2.18 GB/s.)
```
what's why SELECT with join with engine Null is fast.

---------------------
Clickhouse `JOIN` does not use indexes, Clickhouse `IN` uses indexes.

```sql
select count() from left inner join right using A;
1 row in set. Elapsed: 0.367 sec. Processed 100.00 million rows, 800.00 MB (272.56 million rows/s., 2.18 GB/s.)

select count() from left inner join right using B;
1 row in set. Elapsed: 1.030 sec. Processed 100.00 million rows, 2.84 GB (97.12 million rows/s., 2.76 GB/s.)

select count() from left where A in (select A from right);
1 row in set. Elapsed: 0.010 sec. Processed 8.19 thousand rows, 65.54 KB (856.87 thousand rows/s., 6.85 MB/s.)

select count() from left where B in (select B from right);
1 row in set. Elapsed: 0.932 sec. Processed 100.00 million rows, 2.84 GB (107.29 million rows/s., 3.05 GB/s.)
```
`where A in (` is fast because it uses primary index of the `left`

