@alexey-milovidov - apologies, how very rude of me to not follow up on my previous comment after resolving the issue 😄 For the sake of completeness, I'll write it down here so perhaps it can help someone else in future. 

The problem I was facing was actually due to the files having RANDOM dates... this was because I was generating test data to simulate "real world" load but the oversight was that I was using random dates stretching across hundreds of years all within each file being loaded. I would start with an empty database but in a very short timeframe I had generated thousands of "date" partitions... each row in the CSV had to be put into a different partition and this was killing performance (as a side note we have 3x replicas for each shard located in different continents which is also "not recommended" in terms of performance however it is a business requirement for us).

After using more "real world" test data and later production data ClickHouse started behaving as expected 😂and I'm also glad to say we've had ClickHouse loading CSVs in production for several months and reading the results via MySQL Protocol through ProxySQL without any hiccups!

